## Goal
Fix false-positive ArgTypeMismatch when callers skip defaulted params via named arguments.

## Source
todo-false-positives.txt — Case 1 (2026-04-20, tm-draw-tests)

## Repro
```angelscript
void AddIndentedTooltip(const string &in msg, bool pushFont = false, float w = -1.0) { ... }

AddIndentedTooltip("...", w: 20.0);
```

## LSP today
`src/GraphTab.as:261:132: error: argument 2 of AddIndentedTooltip: expected bool, got float`

## Reality
Game-side AngelScript accepts `w: 20.0` as the third parameter and compiles cleanly.

## Root cause
- Parser drops names in `parse_call_argument` (name is eaten, only value kept; AST has no slot).
- `walk_args_and_check_types` binds args positionally.
- Param names already exist in `SymbolKind::Function { params: Vec<(name, type_text)> }`.

## Acceptance
- [ ] Call args preserve optional parameter name in AST
- [ ] Named args map to the matching parameter (skip intermediate defaults)
- [ ] Regression test for `f(msg, w: 20.0)` with signature `(string, bool=false, float=-1.0)` produces 0 ArgTypeMismatch
- [ ] Mixed positional + named still works; unknown name is diagnosed (or silently skipped if AS does)

## Notes
Highest-trust fix: false positives train users to ignore the LSP.